# Finite witnesses for the two connected orbital graphs

Rows enumerate the orbits of ordered pairs (0,8) and (1,3), each of valency 45.
Neighbors have distinct central-block labels. A spanning forest has roots 0
and 1 and depth at most four. These tables are only data; `GraphChecks` proves
all identities used in the block-kernel argument by kernel reduction.
See `ProjectiveComparison/source/replay.py` for reproducible discovery from
the original ATLAS-derived permutations and `BlockData` for source attribution.
